{"id":330,"date":"2016-05-16T12:48:00","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:48:00","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/uk-badminton-find-badminton-clubs-competitions-and-activities-in-england\/"},"modified":"2016-09-01T10:13:37","modified_gmt":"2016-09-01T10:13:37","slug":"uk-badminton-places-to-play-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/uk-badminton-places-to-play.html","title":{"rendered":"UK badminton: Find Badminton Clubs, Competitions and Activities in England"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<div style=\"float: left;\"><\/div>\n<p>To enjoy a good game of badminton, you&#8217;ll need at least 4 people to play doubles. Of course, the more the better!<\/p>\n<p>The problem is it&#8217;s often difficult to look for new badminton friends and games especially when you&#8217;re just starting to pick up the sport or when you have moved to a new place.<\/p>\n<p>Don&#8217;t let this make you retire your racket!<\/p>\n<p>I was raised in Malaysia until I moved to Melbourne, Australia for my studies. There wasn&#8217;t a problem looking for badminton games in Malaysia, considering all my badminton friends were close to me and badminton is a national sport in Malaysia.<\/p>\n<p>I barely knew anyone in Melbourne and I could hardly look for social badminton games to play. Therefore I stopped playing badminton for almost 2 years.<\/p>\n<p>The main problem was that I did not know <em>where<\/em> to look for social badminton games.<\/p>\n<h3>A New Solution<\/h3>\n<p>Badminton England has introduced a revolutionary online portal, <a href=\"http:\/\/www.playbadminton.co.uk\/\" target=\"_blank\">www.PlayBadminton.co.uk<\/a> to help connect casual badminton players in England.<\/p>\n<p>You&#8217;ll be able to look for <strong>badminton clubs, activities, coaching<\/strong> and <strong>competitions<\/strong> around you. The site is convenient to use and has a very sophisticated search function.<\/p>\